Z||000000||DecadenceR||05-26-2001||10:46 AM||||On the firewall of my 84 SE on the lrft hand side, there is a group of 4 relays. 2 on top, 2 right under them. <BR>First question... What are these relays for?<BR>Second question... The left bottom relay... when th wiring is cliped into it, I don't notice anything different from when it's unplugged. But, if I step on the brakes, when the relay is plugged in only, the brake lights don't go off. What's up with that?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rodrv6||05-26-2001||11:07 AM||||One of the top relays is the fuel pump relay, the other one is the A/C clutch relay.  The two bottom relays are a little strange.  They operate the brake lights and turn signals in the tail lights, but only the very outside bulb on each side!  There are 3 stop/turn bulbs in each tail light.  The inner two bulbs are wired straight into the turn signal and brake light switch.  For some reason GM decided they needed a relay to operate the outside bulbs.  The left lower relay is for the left tail light, and the right lower is for the right tail light.  I had a similar problem on my 84 when one of the relays would stick and leave one of the brake lights on until I smacked it.  Finally changed it and problem solved.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
Z||000002||DecadenceR||05-26-2001||06:05 PM||||Okay, so to get these relays, what would I ask for when I went to GM? Tail light relays? Or would they be under another weird name like evrything else is?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rodrv6||05-26-2001||09:48 PM||||I'd take one of them out and tell the parts guy to get "one of these"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
